# =============================================================================
# Job Paglu frontend - environment template
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS FILE IS
#   The frontend's own variable set, kept separate from the repository-root
#   .env.example on purpose.
#
#   Astro splits environment variables into two security classes:
#     * `PUBLIC_`-prefixed - inlined into the client bundle and readable by
#       anyone who opens devtools. Treat every one of these as published.
#     * everything else     - available during SSR only (server code and the
#       Astro config), never sent to the browser.
#
#   Keeping the frontend's variables in their own file makes that boundary
#   visible. Nothing in this file is a secret, and nothing secret may be added
#   to it: the frontend never holds a database URL, a session secret or an API
#   key. It talks to the Go API, and the API holds the secrets.
#
#   Copy it, then fill it in:
#       bash:        cp .env.example .env
#       PowerShell:  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#
#   `.env` is git-ignored. The declared types for these variables live in
#   src/env.d.ts (owned by the frontend code, not by this file).
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The three-way API URL split
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There are three variables and they are three different answers to "where is
# the API?", asked by three different callers. In production they are NOT the
# same value, and that is the whole point.
#
#   PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL  what the BROWSER fetches. In production this is the
#                        site's OWN origin, so admin calls go to /api/* on the
#                        page's origin, the session cookie is first-party, and
#                        CORS never engages. src/lib/api.ts uses this and only
#                        this in the browser.
#
#   API_BASE_URL         what SSR fetches. Points straight at the API project,
#                        so rendering a public job page does not bounce through
#                        the /api/* route. src/lib/api.ts prefers this on the
#                        server.
#
#   API_PROXY_TARGET     where src/pages/api/[...path].ts forwards to. Same API
#                        origin. Read at build time only, never from a request,
#                        so the proxy cannot be aimed elsewhere by a caller.
#                        NOT NEEDED in the documented Vercel deployment: the
#                        vercel.json rewrite handles /api/* and that Astro route
#                        is the inert fallback. Set it only if you switch.
#
# Production (single origin - the recommended topology):
#   PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://home.jobpaglu.eu.cc
#   API_BASE_URL=https://REPLACE-API-PROJECT.vercel.app
# and on the backend: FRONTEND_URL=https://home.jobpaglu.eu.cc
#
# Locally all three are just the backend on localhost, so the proxy is a no-op
# pass-through and you can test either path.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base origin of the Go API as the BROWSER should reach it. Scheme included, no
# trailing slash. Inlined into the client bundle: the admin dashboard runs in
# the browser and must know where to send its fetches. A URL, not a secret.
# In production set this to the SITE's origin, not the API project URL - see above.
# Required: YES. No default - src/lib/api.ts throws a clear error if it is unset.
PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Server-side override, used during SSR only. Lets the server-rendering function
# (or a container) reach the API over a different hostname while the browser
# keeps using the site's own. Falls back to PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL when unset.
# Locally these are the same value, so you can normally delete this line; it is
# shown because docker-compose's `full` profile does need it (the container
# reaches the backend at http://backend:8080, the browser at localhost), and
# because in production it is what keeps SSR off the proxy hop.
# Required: no (but set it in production). Default: PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL
API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Upstream origin for the /api/* Astro proxy route. Server-only, never exposed
# to the browser. Falls back to API_BASE_URL.
#
# NOT NEEDED in the documented Vercel deployment: /api/* is handled by the
# rewrite in frontend/vercel.json, which is matched before filesystem routes, so
# the Astro route never runs. It is kept as the platform-independent fallback -
# set this only if you remove the rewrite. Only one of the two should ever be
# active. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
# Required: no. Default: API_BASE_URL
API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8080

# Absolute public origin of this site. Drives canonical links, Open Graph URLs
# and sitemap.xml, and is read by astro.config.mjs at build time. Set it per
# environment so a preview deployment emits its own canonicals instead of
# pointing search engines at production.
# Required: no. Default (in astro.config.mjs): https://jobpaglu.com
SITE_URL=http://localhost:4321

# Which environment the frontend believes it is in. Gates development-only
# affordances. Must not be used to gate anything security-relevant - the value
# is visible to the client if it is ever exposed with a PUBLIC_ prefix.
# Required: no. Default: production. Values: development | production
APP_ENV=development
